    "root_cause": "The lower-bound-only validation of `iCol` (checking only `iCol < 1`) fails to prevent arbitrarily large column numbers read from a corrupt FTS3 database. The missing upper-bound check allows values large enough to trigger a 32-bit size_t overflow in the subsequent `sizeof(struct Fts3auxColstats) * (iCol+2)` multiplication inside fts3auxGrowStatArray, causing an undersized heap allocation. The commit bb0c54283d introduced this pattern as a partial crash fix without considering the integer overflow risk from excessively large column numbers.",
